<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kendujhar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Keonjhar, Keonjhargarh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kendujhar, also known as Keonjhar or Keonjhargarh, is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the headquarters of Kendujhar district. It was the capital of the princely state of Keonjhar until it merged with Odisha in 1948. The district is rich in iron ore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kendujhar.jpg" alt="Kendujhar" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JAGANNATH MAHAPRABHU 2006 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kendujhargarh_palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
